In order to appreciate two concepts pecuniary damages may include expenses incurred by the Nishat(Dar) vs Pushpender(184/18Jn) on 7 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/130137710/
10 claimant: (i) medical attendance; (ii) loss of earning of profit up to the date of trial;
(iii) other material loss.

This means that the Tribunal should consider and decide with reference to the evidence:
(i) whether the disablement is permanent or temporary;
(ii) if the disablement is permanent, whether it is permanent total disablement or permanent partial disablement;
(iii) if the disablement percentage is expressed with MACT No.1701/2024 Nishad @
Raju Vs. Pushpender & Ors.. Page No. 25 of 49 reference to any specific limb, then the effect of such disablement of the limb on the functioning of the entire body, that is, the permanent disability suffered by the person.

Accordingly, it is directed that the compensation towards loss of dependency shall be assessed by taking minimum wages as notified by the Government of NCT of Delhi for the relevant period,
that is 04.12.2017 for a skilled worker; 40% is to be added towards future prospects to such income;
multiplier shall be 18.
